---
/**
 * "How it was built" — la página de proceso del TFM.
 *
 * ⚠️ Reordenada 2026-09-04 sobre AX-10: la versión anterior abría con trece
 * decisiones elegidas por ser interesantes para quien escribe la página, no
 * para quien contrata. Ahora abre con el TRABAJO — el flujo y cómo se ganó la
 * precisión — y las decisiones vienen detrás como la parte explicada.
 *
 * Dos decisiones y en este orden: primero la de código (arquitectura pensada
 * para que la integración no cueste nada), que es lo que lee un equipo
 * técnico; luego la mejor del proyecto (booleanos para enfocar al modelo y el
 * nivel derivado por código).
 *
 * ⛔ Sólo cifras de ingeniería: el hallazgo del catálogo es material del
 * manuscrito con el laboratorio y no es sólo de Marc para publicarlo.
 *
 * Figuras dibujadas desde los tokens (AX-8). Presupuesto AX-9: 240 s.
 */
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import PipelineFlow from "../../../components/figures/PipelineFlow.astro";
import BenchmarkArc from "../../../components/figures/BenchmarkArc.astro";
import DecisionCard from "../../../components/ui/DecisionCard.astro";
import { withBase } from "../../../utils/url";
import { LINKS } from "../../../consts";
---

<Base
  title="How the thesis was built"
  description="The workflow behind an LLM-plus-deterministic-code pipeline for grapevine gene curation, how its accuracy was won, and the two design decisions that carry it."
>
  <article class="proc">
    <div class="container proc__wrap">
      <a class="proc__back" href={withBase("/work/tfm")}>← Back to the thesis</a>

      <header class="proc__header">
        <span class="mono-label">Data-science thesis · how it was built</span>
        <h1>How it was built, and how the accuracy was won</h1>
        <p class="proc__lede">
          The thesis page says what the pipeline does. This one shows how I
          work: the flow I built, how its accuracy climbed, and the two decisions
          I'd defend in an interview.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- 1 · El trabajo primero -->
      <section class="proc__phase reveal">
        <h2 class="proc__phase-title">The flow I built</h2>
        <p class="proc__body">
          A paper goes in; an evidence-graded row comes out. The model appears
          twice and is bracketed by code both times, and the expert sits at the
          two points where being wrong is expensive.
        </p>
        <PipelineFlow />
      </section>

      <!-- 2 · Cómo se ganó la precisión -->
      <section class="proc__phase reveal">
        <h2 class="proc__phase-title">How the accuracy was won</h2>
        <p class="proc__body">
          None of it was right first time. I benchmarked broadly, found the
          ambiguity concentrated rather than spread, grew the hand-curated gold
          set family by family, and changed the unit the classifier works on.
        </p>
        <BenchmarkArc />
      </section>

      <!-- 3 · Las decisiones, como la parte explicada -->
      <section class="proc__phase reveal">
        <h2 class="proc__phase-title">The two decisions behind it</h2>

        <DecisionCard
          n="01"
          title="Built so that integrating it costs the receiving team nothing"
          discarded="A single application with the interface, the rules and the database access in one place — faster to demo, and what the deadline wanted."
          cost="More boundaries to respect, and an integration step that has to be run deliberately instead of happening implicitly."
        >
          <p>
            Every stage is a module; the benchmark harness imports from the
            production package and never the other way round. The entry points —
            two command-line tools and a local API — carry no domain logic at
            all: they wire configuration to modules and nothing else.
          </p>
          <p>
            The part I planned for early is the interface. It is a pure facade
            with <strong>zero domain rules in it</strong>, and it adopts the
            receiving platform's own component library and folder conventions
            from the first commit. So the curation app drops into their monorepo
            rather than being ported into it — and the UI can be replaced
            outright, standalone or otherwise, without touching a line of the
            package underneath.
          </p>
        </DecisionCard>

        <DecisionCard
          n="02"
          title="Booleans to focus the model; the level derived by code"
          discarded="Letting the model read the paper and return the evidence level — one call, and far less to build."
          cost="Every question has to be written, calibrated and tested on its own."
        >
          <p>
            The deliverable is an evidence level on a published scale, and a
            level is exactly what a reviewer will want to challenge. So the model
            never produces one. It answers a fixed set of yes/no questions about
            what the paper reports, and tested code turns those answers into the
            level. Of roughly thirty output columns, fourteen come from the
            model; the rest is code.
          </p>
          <p>
            What that buys is not tidiness. The level can be re-derived from
            stored answers without calling the model again, audited line by line,
            corrected at the rule instead of at the output — and unit-tested,
            which an opinion cannot be. The derivation lives in exactly one
            place, held there by a test, because a divergent copy once promoted a
            level it should not have.
          </p>
        </DecisionCard>
      </section>

      <!-- 4 · La puerta -->
      <section class="proc__doors" aria-labelledby="proc-doors">
        <h2 id="proc-doors" class="proc__phase-title">Where this goes next</h2>
        <p class="proc__body">
          The thesis defends in January, so the findings aren't up here: they
          belong to the manuscript and to the group I built this with. The
          engineering is mine to show, and it's what's on this page.
        </p>
        <a class="proc__cta" href={`mailto:${LINKS.email}`}>
          Ask me about the parts that aren't here
          <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .proc {
    padding-block: var(--space-xl) var(--space-2xl);
    /* AX-12 · atmósfera de capítulo en el suelo; el acento no se toca. */
    --ground-2: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 7%, var(--paper));
    --ground-tint: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 11%, var(--paper));
    --ground-rule: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 38%, var(--line));
  }
  .proc__wrap {
    max-width: 54rem;
  }
  .proc__back {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .proc__header {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    border-bottom: var(--border);
  }
  .proc__header h1 {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
  }
  .proc__lede {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .proc__phase {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
  }
  .proc__phase > :global(figure) {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .proc__phase-title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 30%, transparent);
  }
  .proc__body {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
  }

  .proc__doors {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
    border-top: var(--border);
  }
  .proc__cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 40%, var(--line));
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 7%, var(--paper));
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--accent-deep);
    transition: gap var(--dur) var(--ease), background var(--dur) var(--ease),
      border-color var(--dur) var(--ease);
  }
  .proc__cta:hover {
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 13%, var(--paper));
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
